         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Very many TEI elements take the value <inline font-style="italic">type</inline> (see the specification for <inline color="black" font-family="Helvetica">att.typed</inline> for a full list). In most cases, no constraint is placed on the possible values for this attribute. In the case of the element <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.name" text-decoration="underline">&lt;name&gt;</basic-link> however, the possible values for this attribute are limited as indicated below: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.name" text-decoration="underline">name</basic-link>
                        </inline> (name, proper noun) contains a proper noun or noun phrase.<table text-align="left"
                               font-size="9pt"
                               table-layout="fixed"
                               width="100%"
                               id="d27e3817">
                           <table-body text-indent="0pt">
                              <table-row>
                                 <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                                    <block>
                                       <inline font-style="italic">type</inline>
                                    </block>
                                 </table-cell>
                                 <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                                    <block>characterizes the element in some sense, using any convenient classification scheme or typology.</block>
                                 </table-cell>
                              </table-row>
                           </table-body>
                        </table>
                     </block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
            <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="42pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">person</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>person</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">forename</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>forename</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">surname</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>surname</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">personGenName</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>generational name component</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">personRoleName</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>role or position in society</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">personAddName</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>additional name component (e.g. nickname)</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">nameLink</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>connecting link within a name (e.g. van der)</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">org</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>organization</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">country</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>country</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">placeGeog</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>geographical name</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">place</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>place</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="Simple-composite"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="18pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="6pt"
                space-before.optimum="12pt"
                text-indent="0em">12. Composite and Floating Texts</block>
         <block line-height="1">A composite text, like a simple text, has an optional front and back matter. In between however, instead of a single body, it contains one or more discrete texts, each with its own optional front and back matter. The following elements are provided to handle composite texts of various kinds. <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.group" text-decoration="underline">group</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains the body of a composite text, grouping together a sequence of distinct texts (or groups of such texts) which are regarded as a unit for some purpose, for example the collected works of an author, a sequence of prose essays, etc.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.floatingText" text-decoration="underline">floatingText</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a single text of any kind, whether unitary or composite, which interrupts the text containing it at any point and after which the surrounding text resumes.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.teiCorpus" text-decoration="underline">teiCorpus</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains the whole of a TEI encoded corpus, comprising a single corpus header and one or more TEI elements, each containing a single text header and a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">A typical example might be an anthology containing several distinct works, or any other kind of collection, encoded using an overall structure like this: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;teiHeader&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ header information for the composite ]--&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/teiHeader&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;text&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;front&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ front matter for the composite  ]--&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/front&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;group&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;text&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;front&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ front matter of first text ]--&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;/front&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;body&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ body of first text  ]--&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;/body&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;back&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ back matter of first text ]--&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;/back&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;/text&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;text&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;front&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ front matter of second text]--&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;/front&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;body&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ body of second text  ]--&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;/body&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;back&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ back matter of second text ]--&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;/back&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;/text&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ more texts or groups of texts here ]--&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/group&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;back&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[ back matter for the composite  ]--&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/back&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/text&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/TEI&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">A different kind of composite text occurs when one text is embedded within another, as for example in the <inline font-style="italic">Arabian Nights</inline> or similar collections of stories, or in other cases where one narrative is interrupted by another. The element <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.floatingText" text-decoration="underline">&lt;floatingText&gt;</basic-link> may be preferred to encode such materials as the following: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>The Gentleman having finish'd his Story, Galecia waited on him to the Stairs-head;
 and at her return, casting her Eyes on the Table, she saw lying there an old dirty
 rumpled Book, and found in it the following story:<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;floatingText&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;body&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>IN the time of the Holy War when Christians from all parts went into the Holy
     Land to oppose the Turks; Amongst these there was a certain English Knight...<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- rest of story here --&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>The King graciously pardoned the Knight; Richard was kindly receiv'd into his
     Convent, and all things went on in good order: But from hence came the Proverb, We
     must not strike <inline>&lt;hi&gt;</inline>Robert<inline>&lt;/hi&gt;</inline> for <inline>&lt;hi&gt;</inline>Richard.<inline>&lt;/hi&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/body&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/floatingText&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;pb n="43"/&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>By this time Galecia's Maid brought up her Supper; after which she cast her Eyes
 again on the foresaid little Book, where she found the following Story ....<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Note that there is only a single TEI header for composite texts of either kind, since the assumption is that the composite is at some level describable as a single work. However, it is also possible to define a composite of complete TEI texts, each with its own TEI header. Such a collection is known as a <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">TEI corpus</inline>, and must itself have a TEI header: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;teiCorpus xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;teiHeader&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[header information for the corpus]--&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/teiHeader&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;TEI&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;teiHeader&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[header information for first text]--&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/teiHeader&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;text&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[first text in corpus]--&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/text&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/TEI&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;TEI&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;teiHeader&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[header information for second text]--&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/teiHeader&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;text&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!--[second text in corpus]--&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/text&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/TEI&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/teiCorpus&gt;</inline>
            </block> It is also possible to create a composite of corpora -- that is, one <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.teiCorpus" text-decoration="underline">&lt;teiCorpus&gt;</basic-link> element may contain many nested <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.teiCorpus" text-decoration="underline">&lt;teiCorpus&gt;</basic-link> elements rather than many nested <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.TEI" text-decoration="underline">&lt;TEI&gt;</basic-link> elements, to any depth considered necessary.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="Simple-fronbac"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="18pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="6pt"
                space-before.optimum="12pt"
                text-indent="0em">13. Front and Back Matter</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e3957"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="14pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="3pt"
                space-before.optimum="9pt"
                text-indent="0em">13.1. Front Matter</block>
         <block line-height="1">For many purposes, particularly in older texts, the preliminary material such as title pages, prefatory epistles, etc., may provide very useful additional linguistic or social information.The TEI Guidelines provide a set of recommendations for distinguishing the textual elements most commonly encountered in front matter, which are summarized here.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="h51"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">13.1.1. Title Page</block>
         <block line-height="1">The start of a title page should be marked with the element <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.titlePage" text-decoration="underline">&lt;titlePage&gt;</basic-link>. All text contained on the page should be transcribed and tagged with the appropriate element from the following list: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.titlePage" text-decoration="underline">titlePage</basic-link>
                        </inline> (title page) contains the title page of a text, appearing within the front or back matter.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.docTitle" text-decoration="underline">docTitle</basic-link>
                        </inline> (document title) contains the title of a document, including all its constituents, as given on a title page.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.titlePart" text-decoration="underline">titlePart</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a subsection or division of the title of a work, as indicated on a title page.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.byline" text-decoration="underline">byline</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains the primary statement of responsibility given for a work on its title page or at the head or end of the work.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.docAuthor" text-decoration="underline">docAuthor</basic-link>
                        </inline> (document author) contains the name of the author of the document, as given on the title page (often but not always contained in a byline).</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.docDate" text-decoration="underline">docDate</basic-link>
                        </inline> (document date) contains the date of a document, as given on a title page or in a dateline.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.docEdition" text-decoration="underline">docEdition</basic-link>
                        </inline> (document edition) contains an edition statement as presented on a title page of a document.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.docImprint" text-decoration="underline">docImprint</basic-link>
                        </inline> (document imprint) contains the imprint statement (place and date of publication, publisher name), as given (usually) at the foot of a title page.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.epigraph" text-decoration="underline">epigraph</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a quotation, anonymous or attributed, appearing at the start or end of a section or on a title page.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Typeface distinctions should be marked with the <inline font-style="italic">rendition </inline> attribute when necessary, as described above though a very detailed description of the letter spacing and sizing used in ornamental titles is not easily done. Changes of language should be marked by appropriate use of the <inline font-style="italic">xml:lang</inline> attribute or the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.foreign" text-decoration="underline">&lt;foreign&gt;</basic-link> element, as necessary. Names of people, places, or organizations, may be tagged using the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.name" text-decoration="underline">&lt;name&gt;</basic-link> element wherever they appear if no other more specific element is available.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Two example title pages follow: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;titlePage&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;docTitle&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;titlePart type="main"&gt;</inline>PARADISE REGAIN'D. A POEM In IV
  <inline>&lt;hi&gt;</inline>BOOKS<inline>&lt;/hi&gt;</inline>.<inline>&lt;/titlePart&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;titlePart&gt;</inline>To which is added <inline>&lt;title&gt;</inline>SAMSON AGONISTES<inline>&lt;/title&gt;</inline>.<inline>&lt;/titlePart&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/docTitle&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;byline&gt;</inline>The Author <inline>&lt;docAuthor&gt;</inline>JOHN MILTON<inline>&lt;/docAuthor&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/byline&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;docImprint&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>LONDON<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>, Printed by <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>J.M.<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline> for <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>John
     Starkey<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline> at the <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>Mitre<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline> in <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>Fleetstreet<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>, near
 <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>Temple-Bar.<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/docImprint&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;docDate&gt;</inline>MDCLXXI<inline>&lt;/docDate&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/titlePage&gt;</inline>
            </block>
            <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;titlePage&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;docTitle&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;titlePart type="main"&gt;</inline>Lives of the Queens of England, from the Norman
     Conquest;<inline>&lt;/titlePart&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;titlePart type="sub"&gt;</inline>with anecdotes of their courts.<inline>&lt;/titlePart&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/docTitle&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;titlePart&gt;</inline>Now first published from Official Records and other authentic documents
   private as well as public.<inline>&lt;/titlePart&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;docEdition&gt;</inline>New edition, with corrections and additions<inline>&lt;/docEdition&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;byline&gt;</inline>By <inline>&lt;docAuthor&gt;</inline>Agnes Strickland<inline>&lt;/docAuthor&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/byline&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;epigraph&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;q&gt;</inline>The treasures of antiquity laid up in old historic rolls, I opened.<inline>&lt;/q&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;bibl&gt;</inline>BEAUMONT<inline>&lt;/bibl&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/epigraph&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;docImprint&gt;</inline>Philadelphia: Blanchard and Lea<inline>&lt;/docImprint&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;docDate&gt;</inline>1860.<inline>&lt;/docDate&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/titlePage&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">As elsewhere, the <inline font-style="italic">ref</inline> attribute may be used to link a name with a canonical definition of the entity being named. For example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;byline&gt;</inline>By <inline>&lt;docAuthor&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;name ref="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agnes_Strickland"&gt;</inline>Agnes Strickland<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/docAuthor&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/byline&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="h52"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">13.1.2. Prefatory Matter</block>
         <block line-height="1">Major blocks of text within the front matter should be marked using <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.div" text-decoration="underline">&lt;div&gt;</basic-link> elements; the following suggested values for the <inline font-style="italic">type</inline> attribute may be used to distinguish various common types of prefatory matter: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="42pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">preface</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A foreword or preface addressed to the reader in which the author or publisher explains the content, purpose, or origin of the text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">dedication</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A formal offering or dedication of a text to one or more persons or institutions by the author.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">abstract</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A summary of the content of a text as continuous prose.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">ack</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A formal declaration of acknowledgment by the author in which persons and institutions are thanked for their part in the creation of a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">contents</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A table of contents, specifying the structure of a work and listing its constituents. The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.list" text-decoration="underline">&lt;list&gt;</basic-link> element should be used to mark its structure.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">frontispiece</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A pictorial frontispiece, possibly including some text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Where other kinds of prefatory matter are encountered, the encoder is at liberty to invent other values for the <inline font-style="italic">type</inline> attribute.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="h52x"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">13.1.3. Liminal Elements</block>
         <block line-height="1">All text divisions, whether in front matter or elsewhere, may begin and end with one or more components which we term <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">liminal elements</inline>, because they begin or end the division. A typical example is a heading or title of some kind which should be tagged using the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.head" text-decoration="underline">&lt;head&gt;</basic-link> element; but there are many other possibilities: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.salute" text-decoration="underline">salute</basic-link>
                        </inline> (salutation) contains a salutation or greeting prefixed to a foreword, dedicatory epistle, or other division of a text, or the salutation in the closing of a letter, preface, etc.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.signed" text-decoration="underline">signed</basic-link>
                        </inline> (signature) contains the closing salutation, etc., appended to a foreword, dedicatory epistle, or other division of a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.byline" text-decoration="underline">byline</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains the primary statement of responsibility given for a work on its title page or at the head or end of the work.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.dateline" text-decoration="underline">dateline</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a brief description of the place, date, time, etc. of production of a letter, newspaper story, or other work, prefixed or suffixed to it as a kind of heading or trailer.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.argument" text-decoration="underline">argument</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a formal list or prose description of the topics addressed by a subdivision of a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.cit" text-decoration="underline">cit</basic-link>
                        </inline> (cited quotation) contains a quotation from some other document, together with a bibliographic reference to its source. In a dictionary it may contain an example text with at least one occurrence of the word form, used in the sense being described, or a translation of the headword, or an example.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.imprimatur" text-decoration="underline">imprimatur</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a formal statement authorizing the publication of a work, sometimes required to appear on a title page or its verso.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.opener" text-decoration="underline">opener</basic-link>
                        </inline> groups together dateline, byline, salutation, and similar phrases appearing as a preliminary group at the start of a division, especially of a letter.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.closer" text-decoration="underline">closer</basic-link>
                        </inline> groups together salutations, datelines, and similar phrases appearing as a final group at the end of a division, especially of a letter.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.postscript" text-decoration="underline">postscript</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a postscript, e.g. to a letter.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">As an example, the beginning and end of the dedication to Milton's <inline font-style="italic">Comus</inline> might be marked up as follows: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;div type="dedication"&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;head&gt;</inline>To the Right Honourable <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>JOHN Lord Viscount BRACLY<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>, Son and Heir
   apparent to the Earl of Bridgewater, &amp;amp;c.<inline>&lt;/head&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;salute&gt;</inline>MY LORD,<inline>&lt;/salute&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>THis <inline>&lt;hi&gt;</inline>Poem<inline>&lt;/hi&gt;</inline>, which receiv'd its first occasion of Birth from your Self,
   and others of your Noble Family .... and as in this representation your
   attendant <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>Thyrsis<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>, so now in all reall expression<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;closer&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;salute&gt;</inline>Your faithfull, and most humble servant<inline>&lt;/salute&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;signed&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>H. LAWES.<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/signed&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/closer&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/div&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e4292"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="14pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="3pt"
                space-before.optimum="9pt"
                text-indent="0em">13.2. Back Matter</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e4294"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">13.2.1. Structural Divisions of Back Matter</block>
         <block line-height="1">Because of variations in publishing practice, back matter can contain virtually any of the elements listed above for front matter, and the same elements should be used where this is so. Additionally, back matter may contain the following types of matter within the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.back" text-decoration="underline">&lt;back&gt;</basic-link> element. Like the structural divisions of the body, these should be marked as <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.div" text-decoration="underline">&lt;div&gt;</basic-link> elements, and distinguished by the following suggested values of the <inline font-style="italic">type</inline> attribute: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="42pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">appendix</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>An ancillary self-contained section of a work, often providing additional but in some sense extra-canonical text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">glossary</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A list of terms associated with definition texts (‘glosses’): this should be encoded as a <inline>&lt;list type="gloss"&gt;</inline> element.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">notes</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A section in which textual or other kinds of notes are gathered together.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">bibliogr</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A list of bibliographic citations: this should be encoded as a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listBibl" text-decoration="underline">&lt;listBibl&gt;</basic-link>.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">index</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>Any form of pre-existing index to the work</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">colophon</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>A statement appearing at the end of a book describing the conditions of its physical production.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="specfronbac"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">13.2.2. Specialized Front and Back Matter</block>
         <block line-height="1">TEI simplePrint also provides elements for some additional components of front or back matter which are characteristic of particular kinds of text, in particular old play texts. These often include lists of dramatis personae and notes about the setting of a play, for which the following elements are provided: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.castList" text-decoration="underline">castList</basic-link>
                        </inline> (cast list) contains a single cast list or dramatis personae.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.castItem" text-decoration="underline">castItem</basic-link>
                        </inline> (cast list item) contains a single entry within a cast list, describing either a single role or a list of non-speaking roles.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.castGroup" text-decoration="underline">castGroup</basic-link>
                        </inline> (cast list grouping) groups one or more individual castItem elements within a cast list.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.role" text-decoration="underline">role</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains the name of a dramatic role, as given in a cast list.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.roleDesc" text-decoration="underline">roleDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (role description) describes a character's role in a drama.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.actor" text-decoration="underline">actor</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains the name of an actor appearing within a cast list.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.set" text-decoration="underline">set</basic-link>
                        </inline> (setting) contains a description of the setting, time, locale, appearance, etc., of the action of a play, typically found in the front matter of a printed performance text (not a stage direction).</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Note that these elements are intended for use in marking up cast lists and setting notes as they appear in a source document. They are not intended for use when marking up definitive lists of the different roles identified in a play, except in so far as that may have been their original purpose.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The following example shows one way of encoding the last part of Shakespeare's <inline font-style="italic">Tempest</inline>, as printed in the first folio:</block>
         <block font-family="Courier"
                background-color="lightgray"
                color="black"
                white-space-treatment="preserve"
                linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                white-space-collapse="false"
                wrap-option="no-wrap"
                text-indent="0em"
                hyphenate="false"
                start-indent="12pt"
                text-align="start"
                font-size="6pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                space-after.optimum="4pt">
            <inline>&lt;back&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;div type="epilogue"&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;head&gt;</inline>Epilogue, spoken by Prospero.<inline>&lt;/head&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;sp&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;l&gt;</inline>Now my Charmes are all ore-throwne,<inline>&lt;/l&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;l&gt;</inline>And what strength I have's mine owne<inline>&lt;/l&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;l&gt;</inline>As you from crimes would pardon'd be,<inline>&lt;/l&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;l&gt;</inline>Let your Indulgence set me free.<inline>&lt;/l&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/sp&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;stage&gt;</inline>Exit<inline>&lt;/stage&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/div&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;set&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>The Scene, an un-inhabited Island.<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/set&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;castList&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;head&gt;</inline>Names of the Actors.<inline>&lt;/head&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;castItem&gt;</inline>Alonso, K. of Naples<inline>&lt;/castItem&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;castItem&gt;</inline>Sebastian, his Brother.<inline>&lt;/castItem&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;castItem&gt;</inline>Prospero, the right Duke of Millaine.<inline>&lt;/castItem&gt;</inline>
            <inline>&lt;!-- etc --&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/castList&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;trailer&gt;</inline>FINIS<inline>&lt;/trailer&gt;</inline>
            <inline>&lt;/back&gt;</inline>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="Simple-fax"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="18pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="6pt"
                space-before.optimum="12pt"
                text-indent="0em">14. Encoding a Digital Facsimile</block>
         <block line-height="1">The following elements may be used to encode a text represented by a collection of digital images, either alone or in conjunction with a textual transcription. <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.facsimile" text-decoration="underline">facsimile</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a representation of some written source in the form of a set of images rather than as transcribed or encoded text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.surface" text-decoration="underline">surface</basic-link>
                        </inline> defines a written surface as a two-dimensional coordinate space, optionally grouping one or more graphic representations of that space, zones of interest within that space, and transcriptions of the writing within them.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.zone" text-decoration="underline">zone</basic-link>
                        </inline> defines any two-dimensional area within a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.surface" text-decoration="underline">&lt;surface&gt;</basic-link> element.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">As mentioned in section <basic-link internal-destination="Simple-figs" text-decoration="underline">9 (Figures and Graphics)</basic-link> above, a TEI simplePrint document may reference a set of page images, alone, or in combination with a transcription. For ease of management, it is strongly recommended that the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.graphic" text-decoration="underline">&lt;graphic&gt;</basic-link> elements representing those page images be grouped together within a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.facsimile" text-decoration="underline">&lt;facsimile&gt;</basic-link> element, as in the following example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;facsimile&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;graphic url="page1.png" xml:id="page1"/&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;graphic url="page2.png" xml:id="page2"/&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/facsimile&gt;</inline>
            </block> If a transcription is supplied in addition, the <inline font-style="italic">xml:id</inline> values can be used to align the page breaks within it with the relevant image, rather than using the URL given on the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.graphic" text-decoration="underline">&lt;graphic&gt;</basic-link> element. <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;text&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- ...--&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;pb facs="#page1"/&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- text contained on page 1 --&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;pb facs="#page2"/&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- text contained on page 2 --&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- ...--&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/text&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.surface" text-decoration="underline">&lt;surface&gt;</basic-link> element is useful in two situations: when it is desired to group different images of the same page, for example of different resolutions; and when it is desired to align parts of a page image with parts of a transcription. The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.zone" text-decoration="underline">&lt;zone&gt;</basic-link> element is used to define (and hence provide an identifier for) the location of a part of an image with reference to the surface on which it appears.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">In this example, a thumbnail and a high resolution image are associated with the same surface: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;facsimile&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;surface&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;graphic xml:id="page1T"
   url="thumbs/page1.png"/&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;graphic xml:id="page1" url="page1.png"/&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/surface&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/facsimile&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">In this example, the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.head" text-decoration="underline">&lt;head&gt;</basic-link> element in the transcription is aligned with the top half of a square image: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;facsimile&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;surface ulx="1" uly="1" lrx="4" lry="4"&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;graphic url="page1.png" xml:id="page1"/&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;zone xml:id="topHalfP1" ulx="1" uly="1"
   lrx="2" lry="4"/&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/surface&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/facsimile&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;text&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;body&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- ... --&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;pb facs="#page1"/&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;head facs="#topHalfP1"&gt;</inline>Text of Heading<inline>&lt;/head&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- ...--&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/body&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/text&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">A more detailed explanation of the use of these attributes and other associated elements is given in the full TEI Guidelines. </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="Simple-header"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="18pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="6pt"
                space-before.optimum="12pt"
                text-indent="0em">15. The Electronic Title Page</block>
         <block line-height="1">Every TEI text has a header which provides information analogous to that provided by the title page of printed text. The header is introduced by the element <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.teiHeader" text-decoration="underline">&lt;teiHeader&gt;</basic-link> and has four major parts: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.fileDesc" text-decoration="underline">fileDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (file description) contains a full bibliographic description of an electronic file.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.encodingDesc" text-decoration="underline">encodingDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (encoding description) documents the relationship between an electronic text and the source or sources from which it was derived.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.profileDesc" text-decoration="underline">profileDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (text-profile description) provides a detailed description of non-bibliographic aspects of a text, specifically the languages and sublanguages used, the situation in which it was produced, the participants and their setting.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.revisionDesc" text-decoration="underline">revisionDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (revision description) summarizes the revision history for a file.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">A corpus or collection of texts with many shared characteristics may have one header for the corpus and individual headers for each component of the corpus. In this case the <inline font-style="italic">type</inline> attribute indicates the type of header. <inline>&lt;teiHeader type="corpus"&gt;</inline> introduces the header for corpus-level information.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Some of the header elements contain running prose which consists of one or more <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.p" text-decoration="underline">&lt;p&gt;</basic-link>s. Others are grouped: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">Elements whose names end in <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">Stmt</inline> (for statement) usually enclose a group of elements recording some structured information.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">Elements whose names end in <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">Decl</inline> (for declaration) enclose information about specific encoding practices.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">Elements whose names end in <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">Desc</inline> (for description) contain a prose description.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e4618"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="14pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="3pt"
                space-before.optimum="9pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.1. The File Description</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.fileDesc" text-decoration="underline">&lt;fileDesc&gt;</basic-link> element is mandatory. It contains a full bibliographic description of the file with the following elements: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.titleStmt" text-decoration="underline">titleStmt</basic-link>
                        </inline> (title statement) groups information about the title of a work and those responsible for its content.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.editionStmt" text-decoration="underline">editionStmt</basic-link>
                        </inline> (edition statement) groups information relating to one edition of a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.extent" text-decoration="underline">extent</basic-link>
                        </inline> describes the approximate size of a text stored on some carrier medium or of some other object, digital or non-digital, specified in any convenient units.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.publicationStmt" text-decoration="underline">publicationStmt</basic-link>
                        </inline> (publication statement) groups information concerning the publication or distribution of an electronic or other text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.seriesStmt" text-decoration="underline">seriesStmt</basic-link>
                        </inline> (series statement) groups information about the series, if any, to which a publication belongs.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.notesStmt" text-decoration="underline">notesStmt</basic-link>
                        </inline> (notes statement) collects together any notes providing information about a text additional to that recorded in other parts of the bibliographic description.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.sourceDesc" text-decoration="underline">sourceDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (source description) describes the source from which an electronic text was derived or generated, typically a bibliographic description in the case of a digitized text, or a phrase such as "born digital" for a text which has no previous existence.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">A minimal TEI header has the following structure: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;teiHeader&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;fileDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;titleStmt&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- [ bibliographic description of the digital resource ] --&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/titleStmt&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;publicationStmt&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- [ information about how the resource is distributed ] --&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/publicationStmt&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;sourceDesc&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;!-- [ information about the sources from which the digital resource is derived ] --&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/sourceDesc&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/fileDesc&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/teiHeader&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e4717"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.1.1. The Title Statement</block>
         <block line-height="1">The following elements can be used in the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.titleStmt" text-decoration="underline">&lt;titleStmt&gt;</basic-link> to provide information about the title of a work and those responsible for its content: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.title" text-decoration="underline">title</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a title for any kind of work.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.author" text-decoration="underline">author</basic-link>
                        </inline> in a bibliographic reference, contains the name(s) of an author, personal or corporate, of a work; for example in the same form as that provided by a recognized bibliographic name authority.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.respStmt" text-decoration="underline">respStmt</basic-link>
                        </inline> (statement of responsibility) supplies a statement of responsibility for the intellectual content of a text, edition, recording, or series, where the specialized elements for authors, editors, etc. do not suffice or do not apply. May also be used to encode information about individuals or organizations which have played a role in the production or distribution of a bibliographic work.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The title of a digital resource derived from a non-digital original may be similar to that of its source but should be distinct from it, for example: <inline font-family="Courier">[title of source]: TEI XML edition</inline> or <inline font-family="Courier">A machine readable version of: [title of source]</inline>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The generic <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.respStmt" text-decoration="underline">&lt;respStmt&gt;</basic-link> element may be used to indicate any kind of responsibility, ranging from a funder or sponsor to an illustrator or editor. It contains the following subcomponents: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.resp" text-decoration="underline">resp</basic-link>
                        </inline> (responsibility) contains a phrase describing the nature of a person's intellectual responsibility, or an organization's role in the production or distribution of a work.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.name" text-decoration="underline">name</basic-link>
                        </inline> (name, proper noun) contains a proper noun or noun phrase.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block> Example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;titleStmt&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;title&gt;</inline>Two stories by Edgar Allen Poe <inline>&lt;/title&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;author&gt;</inline>Poe, Edgar Allen (1809-1849)<inline>&lt;/author&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;respStmt&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;resp&gt;</inline>TEI encoding<inline>&lt;/resp&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>James D. Benson<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/respStmt&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;respStmt&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;resp&gt;</inline>Funding <inline>&lt;/resp&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>Getty Foundation<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/respStmt&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/titleStmt&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e4801"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.1.2. The Edition Statement</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.editionStmt" text-decoration="underline">&lt;editionStmt&gt;</basic-link> groups information relating to one edition of the digital resource (where <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">edition</inline> is used as elsewhere in bibliography), and may include the following elements: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.edition" text-decoration="underline">edition</basic-link>
                        </inline> describes the particularities of one edition of a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.respStmt" text-decoration="underline">respStmt</basic-link>
                        </inline> (statement of responsibility) supplies a statement of responsibility for the intellectual content of a text, edition, recording, or series, where the specialized elements for authors, editors, etc. do not suffice or do not apply. May also be used to encode information about individuals or organizations which have played a role in the production or distribution of a bibliographic work.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;editionStmt&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;edition n="U2"&gt;</inline>Third draft, substantially revised <inline>&lt;date&gt;</inline>1987<inline>&lt;/date&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/edition&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/editionStmt&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Determining exactly what constitutes a new edition of an electronic text is left to the encoder.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e4839"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.1.3. The Extent Statement</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.extent" text-decoration="underline">&lt;extent&gt;</basic-link> statement describes the approximate size of the digital resource.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;extent&gt;</inline>15 Mb
<inline>&lt;/extent&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e4850"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.1.4. The Publication Statement</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.publicationStmt" text-decoration="underline">&lt;publicationStmt&gt;</basic-link> is mandatory. It may contain a simple prose description or groups of the elements described below: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.publisher" text-decoration="underline">publisher</basic-link>
                        </inline> provides the name of the organization responsible for the publication or distribution of a bibliographic item.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.distributor" text-decoration="underline">distributor</basic-link>
                        </inline> supplies the name of a person or other agency responsible for the distribution of a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">At least one of these elements must be present, unless the entire publication statement is in prose. The following elements may occur within them: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.pubPlace" text-decoration="underline">pubPlace</basic-link>
                        </inline> (publication place) contains the name of the place where a bibliographic item was published.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.address" text-decoration="underline">address</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a postal address, for example of a publisher, an organization, or an individual.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.addrLine" text-decoration="underline">addrLine</basic-link>
                        </inline> (address line) contains one line of a postal address.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.idno" text-decoration="underline">idno</basic-link>
                        </inline> (identifier) supplies any form of identifier used to identify some object, such as a bibliographic item, a person, a title, an organization, etc. in a standardized way.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.availability" text-decoration="underline">availability</basic-link>
                        </inline> supplies information about the availability of a text, for example any restrictions on its use or distribution, its copyright status, any licence applying to it, etc.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.licence" text-decoration="underline">licence</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains information about a licence or other legal agreement applicable to the text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.date" text-decoration="underline">date</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a date in any format.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;publicationStmt&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;publisher&gt;</inline>University of Victoria Humanities Computing and Media
   Centre<inline>&lt;/publisher&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;pubPlace&gt;</inline>Victoria, BC<inline>&lt;/pubPlace&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;date&gt;</inline>2011<inline>&lt;/date&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;availability status="restricted"&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;licence target="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/"&gt;</inline> Distributed
     under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported License
  <inline>&lt;/licence&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/availability&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/publicationStmt&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e4956"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.1.5. Series and Notes Statements</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.seriesStmt" text-decoration="underline">&lt;seriesStmt&gt;</basic-link> element groups information about the series, if any, to which a publication belongs. It may contain <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.title" text-decoration="underline">&lt;title&gt;</basic-link>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.idno" text-decoration="underline">&lt;idno&gt;</basic-link>, or <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.respStmt" text-decoration="underline">&lt;respStmt&gt;</basic-link> elements.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.notesStmt" text-decoration="underline">&lt;notesStmt&gt;</basic-link>, if used, contains one or more <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.note" text-decoration="underline">&lt;note&gt;</basic-link> elements which contain a note or annotation. Some information found in the notes area in conventional bibliography has been assigned specific elements in the TEI scheme.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e4980"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.1.6. The Source Description</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.sourceDesc" text-decoration="underline">&lt;sourceDesc&gt;</basic-link> is a mandatory element which records details of the source or sources from which the computer file is derived. It may contain simple prose or a bibliographic citation, using one or more of the following elements: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.bibl" text-decoration="underline">bibl</basic-link>
                        </inline> (bibliographic citation) contains a loosely-structured bibliographic citation of which the sub-components may or may not be explicitly tagged.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listBibl" text-decoration="underline">listBibl</basic-link>
                        </inline> (citation list) contains a list of bibliographic citations of any kind.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Examples: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;sourceDesc&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;bibl&gt;</inline>The first folio of Shakespeare, prepared by Charlton Hinman (The Norton
   Facsimile, 1968)<inline>&lt;/bibl&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/sourceDesc&gt;</inline>
            </block>
            <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;sourceDesc&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;bibl&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;author&gt;</inline>CNN Network News<inline>&lt;/author&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;title&gt;</inline>News headlines<inline>&lt;/title&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;date&gt;</inline>12 Jun 1989<inline>&lt;/date&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/bibl&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/sourceDesc&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e5024"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="14pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="3pt"
                space-before.optimum="9pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.2. The Encoding Description</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.encodingDesc" text-decoration="underline">&lt;encodingDesc&gt;</basic-link> element specifies the methods and editorial principles which governed the transcription of the text. Its use is highly recommended. It may be prose description or may contain more specialized elements chosen from the following list: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.projectDesc" text-decoration="underline">projectDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (project description) describes in detail the aim or purpose for which an electronic file was encoded, together with any other relevant information concerning the process by which it was assembled or collected.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.samplingDecl" text-decoration="underline">samplingDecl</basic-link>
                        </inline> (sampling declaration) contains a prose description of the rationale and methods used in sampling texts in the creation of a corpus or collection.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.editorialDecl" text-decoration="underline">editorialDecl</basic-link>
                        </inline> (editorial practice declaration) provides details of editorial principles and practices applied during the encoding of a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.tagsDecl" text-decoration="underline">tagsDecl</basic-link>
                        </inline> (tagging declaration) provides detailed information about the tagging applied to a document.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.refsDecl" text-decoration="underline">refsDecl</basic-link>
                        </inline> (references declaration) specifies how canonical references are constructed for this text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listPrefixDef" text-decoration="underline">listPrefixDef</basic-link>
                        </inline> (list of prefix definitions) contains a list of definitions of prefixing schemes used in <inline color="black" font-family="Helvetica">data.pointer</inline> values, showing how abbreviated URIs using each scheme may be expanded into full URIs.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.prefixDef" text-decoration="underline">prefixDef</basic-link>
                        </inline> (prefix definition) defines a prefixing scheme used in <inline color="black" font-family="Helvetica">data.pointer</inline> values, showing how abbreviated URIs using the scheme may be expanded into full URIs.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.classDecl" text-decoration="underline">classDecl</basic-link>
                        </inline> (classification declarations) contains one or more taxonomies defining any classificatory codes used elsewhere in the text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.charDecl" text-decoration="underline">charDecl</basic-link>
                        </inline> (character declarations) provides information about nonstandard characters and glyphs.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e5146"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.2.1. Project Description and Sampling Declaration</block>
         <block line-height="1">Examples of <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.projectDesc" text-decoration="underline">&lt;projectDesc&gt;</basic-link> and <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.samplingDecl" text-decoration="underline">&lt;samplingDecl&gt;</basic-link>: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;encodingDesc&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;projectDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>Texts collected for use in the Claremont Shakespeare Clinic, June 1990. <inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/projectDesc&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/encodingDesc&gt;</inline>
            </block>
            <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;encodingDesc&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;samplingDecl&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>Samples of 2000 words taken from the beginning of the text<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/samplingDecl&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/encodingDesc&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e5165"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.2.2. Editorial Declarations</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.editorialDecl" text-decoration="underline">&lt;editorialDecl&gt;</basic-link> contains a prose description of the practices used when encoding the text. Typically this description should cover such topics as the following, each of which may conveniently be given as a separate paragraph: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="42pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">correction </block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>how and under what circumstances corrections have been made in the text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">normalization</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>the extent to which the original source has been regularized or normalized.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">quotation</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>what has been done with quotation marks in the original -- have they been retained or replaced by entity references, are opening and closing quotes distinguished, etc. </block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">hyphenation</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>what has been done with hyphens (especially end-of-line hyphens) in the original -- have they been retained, replaced by entity references, etc.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">segmentation</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>how has the text has been segmented, for example into sentences, tone-units, graphemic strata, etc.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">interpretation</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>what analytic or interpretive information has been added to the text. </block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;editorialDecl&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>The part of speech analysis applied throughout section 4 was added by hand and
   has not been checked.<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>Errors in transcription controlled by using the WordPerfect spelling
   checker.<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>All words converted to Modern American spelling using Webster's 9th Collegiate
   dictionary.<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/editorialDecl&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The full TEI Guidelines provide specialized elements for each of the topics above; these are not however included in TEI simplePrint.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="hdr-rend"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.2.3. Tagging Declaration</block>
         <block line-height="1">When it does not consist simply of a prose description, the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.tagsDecl" text-decoration="underline">&lt;tagsDecl&gt;</basic-link> element may contain a number of more specialized elements providing additional information about how the document concerned has been marked up. The following elements may be used: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.rendition" text-decoration="underline">rendition</basic-link>
                        </inline> supplies information about the rendition or appearance of one or more elements in the source text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.namespace" text-decoration="underline">namespace</basic-link>
                        </inline> supplies the formal name of the namespace to which the elements documented by its children belong.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.tagUsage" text-decoration="underline">tagUsage</basic-link>
                        </inline> documents the usage of a specific element within a specified document.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Here is a simple example, showing how these elements may be used. It indicates the number of times the elements <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.hi" text-decoration="underline">&lt;hi&gt;</basic-link> and <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.title" text-decoration="underline">&lt;title&gt;</basic-link> from the TEI namespace have been used in the document. It also documents how the way that the source document was originally printed has been represented using TEI tagging: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;tagsDecl partial="true"&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;rendition xml:id="rend-bo"&gt;</inline>font-weight:bold<inline>&lt;/rendition&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;rendition xml:id="rend-it"
  selector="hi, title"&gt;</inline>font-style:italic<inline>&lt;/rendition&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;namespace name="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;tagUsage gi="hi" occurs="467"/&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;tagUsage gi="title" occurs="45"/&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/namespace&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/tagsDecl&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.rendition" text-decoration="underline">&lt;rendition&gt;</basic-link> elements here contain fragments expressed in the W3C standard Cascading Stylesheets language (CSS). Their function here is to associate the particular styles concerned with an identifier (for example <inline color="black" font-family="Helvetica">rend-bo</inline>) which can then be pointed to from elsewhere within the document by means of the <inline font-style="italic">rendition</inline> attribute mentioned in section <basic-link internal-destination="faces" text-decoration="underline">3.5.1 (Changes of Typeface, etc.)</basic-link> above. To indicate, for example, that a particular name in the document was rendered in a bold font it might be tagged <inline>&lt;name rendition="#rend-bo"&gt;</inline>. The <inline font-style="italic">selector</inline> attribute used in the preceding example is used to indicate once for all a default rendition value to be associated with several elements: in this example, unless otherwise indicated, it is assumed that the content of each <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.hi" text-decoration="underline">&lt;hi&gt;</basic-link> and each <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.title" text-decoration="underline">&lt;title&gt;</basic-link> element was originally rendered using an italic font.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">For TEI simplePrint, a large set of such rendition definitions has been predefined. The encoder is not therefore required to supply any detailed declarations, but can refer to the predefined list using the following list: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="42pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:allcaps</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>all capitals</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:blackletter</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>black letter or gothic typeface</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:bold</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>bold typeface</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:bottombraced</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>marked with a brace under the bottom of the text</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:boxed</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>border around the text</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:centre</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>centred text</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:cursive</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>cursive typeface</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:display</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>block display</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:doublestrikethrough</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>strikethrough with double line</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:doubleunderline</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>underlined with double line</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:dropcap</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>initial letter larger or decorated</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:float</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>floated out of main flow</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:hyphen</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>with a hyphen here (e.g. in line break)</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:inline</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>inline rendering</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:justify</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>justified text</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:italic</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>italic typeface</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:larger</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>larger type</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:left</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>aligned to the left or left-justified</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:leftbraced</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>marked with a brace on the left side of the text</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:letterspace</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>larger-than-normal spacing between letters, usually for emphasis</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:literal</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>fixed-width typeface, spacing preserved</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:normalstyle</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>upright shape and default weight of typeface</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:normalweight</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>normal typeface weight</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:right</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>aligned to the right or right-justified</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:rightbraced</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>marked with a brace to the right of the text</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:rotateleft</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>rotated to the left</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:rotateright</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>rotated to the right</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:smallcaps</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>small caps</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:smaller</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>smaller type</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:strikethrough</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>strikethrough</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:subscript</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>subscript</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:superscript</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>superscript</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:topbraced</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>marked with a brace above the text</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:typewriter</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>fixed-width typeface, like typewriter</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:underline</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>underlined with single line</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="start"
                            font-weight="bold"
                            keep-together.within-line="always">simple:wavyunderline</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <block> </block>underlined with wavy line</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <inline>simple:</inline> prefix used here must be mapped to a location at which the full rendition declaration can be found, by default the XML source of the present document.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Full details of the way these elements may be used are provided in the relevant section of the TEI Guidelines (<basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/HD.html#HD57)">http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/HD.html#HD57</basic-link>).</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="refsdecl"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.2.4. Reference, Prefix, and Classification Declarations</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.refsDecl" text-decoration="underline">&lt;refsDecl&gt;</basic-link> element is used to document the way in which any standard referencing scheme built into the encoding works. In its simplest form, it consists of prose description.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;refsDecl&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>The <inline>&lt;att&gt;</inline>n<inline>&lt;/att&gt;</inline> attribute on each <inline>&lt;gi&gt;</inline>div<inline>&lt;/gi&gt;</inline> contains the canonical
   reference for each division in the form XX.yyy where XX is the book number in
   roman numeral and yyy is the section number in arabic.<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>Milestone tags refer to the edition of 1830 as E30 and that of 1850 as E50.<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/refsDecl&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listPrefixDef" text-decoration="underline">&lt;listPrefixDef&gt;</basic-link> element contains one or more <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.prefixDef" text-decoration="underline">&lt;prefixDef&gt;</basic-link> elements, each defining a prefix which has been used to abbreviate references to other documents, for example as the value of a <inline font-style="italic">target</inline> or other pointing attribute. The definition provides information about how the prefix can be translated automatically into a full URL, as in the following example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;listPrefixDef&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;prefixDef ident="psn"
  matchPattern="([A-Z]+)"
  replacementPattern="http://www.example.com/personography.xml#$1"/&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/listPrefixDef&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">In this case, a pointer value in the form <inline>psn:MDH</inline> would be translated to <inline font-family="Courier">http://www.example.com/personography.xml#MDH</inline>.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.classDecl" text-decoration="underline">&lt;classDecl&gt;</basic-link> element groups together definitions or sources for any descriptive classification schemes or <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">taxonomies</inline> used by other parts of the header. These schemes may be defined in a number of different ways, using one or more of the following elements: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.taxonomy" text-decoration="underline">taxonomy</basic-link>
                        </inline> defines a typology either implicitly, by means of a bibliographic citation, or explicitly by a structured taxonomy.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.bibl" text-decoration="underline">bibl</basic-link>
                        </inline> (bibliographic citation) contains a loosely-structured bibliographic citation of which the sub-components may or may not be explicitly tagged.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.category" text-decoration="underline">category</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains an individual descriptive category, possibly nested within a superordinate category, within a user-defined taxonomy.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.catDesc" text-decoration="underline">catDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (category description) describes some category within a taxonomy or text typology, either in the form of a brief prose description or in terms of the situational parameters used by the TEI formal <inline hyphenate="false" color="black" font-family="Courier">&lt;textDesc&gt;</inline>.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">In the simplest case, the taxonomy may be defined by a bibliographic reference, as in the following example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;classDecl&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;taxonomy xml:id="LC-SH"&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;bibl&gt;</inline>Library of Congress Subject Headings <inline>&lt;/bibl&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/taxonomy&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/classDecl&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Alternatively, or in addition, the encoder may define a special purpose classification scheme, as in the following example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;taxonomy xml:id="B"&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;bibl&gt;</inline>Brown Corpus<inline>&lt;/bibl&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.A"&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>Press Reportage<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.A1"&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>Daily<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.A2"&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>Sunday<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.A3"&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>National<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.A4"&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>Provincial<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.A5"&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>Political<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.A6"&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>Sports<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.D"&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>Religion<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.D1"&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>Books<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;category xml:id="B.D2"&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;catDesc&gt;</inline>Periodicals and tracts<inline>&lt;/catDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/category&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/taxonomy&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Linkage between a particular text and a category within such a taxonomy is made by means of the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.catRef" text-decoration="underline">&lt;catRef&gt;</basic-link> element within the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.textClass" text-decoration="underline">&lt;textClass&gt;</basic-link> element, as described in the next section.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="chardecl"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="12pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                font-style="italic"
                space-after="2pt"
                space-before.optimum="4pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.2.5. The character declaration</block>
         <block line-height="1">As mentioned in section <basic-link internal-destination="code" text-decoration="underline">5.2 (Formulae, Codes, and Special Characters)</basic-link> above, the element <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.g" text-decoration="underline">&lt;g&gt;</basic-link> is used to indicate the presence of a nonstandard character or glyph in a transcription, and to reference a definition or description of it in the Header. These definitions are provided by means of the following specialised elements given within the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.charDecl" text-decoration="underline">&lt;charDecl&gt;</basic-link> component of the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.encodingDesc" text-decoration="underline">&lt;encodingDesc&gt;</basic-link>
            <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.char" text-decoration="underline">char</basic-link>
                        </inline> (character) provides descriptive information about a character.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.glyph" text-decoration="underline">glyph</basic-link>
                        </inline> (character glyph) provides descriptive information about a character glyph.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.charName" text-decoration="underline">charName</basic-link>
                        </inline> (character name) contains the name of a character, expressed following Unicode conventions.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.glyphName" text-decoration="underline">glyphName</basic-link>
                        </inline> (character glyph name) contains the name of a glyph, expressed following Unicode conventions for character names.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.desc" text-decoration="underline">desc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (description) contains a brief description of the object documented by its parent element, typically a documentation element or an entity.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.mapping" text-decoration="underline">mapping</basic-link>
                        </inline> (character mapping) contains one or more characters which are related to the parent character or glyph in some respect, as specified by the <inline font-style="italic">type</inline> attribute.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block> For example, the alchemical symbol for air might be encoded where it appears in a text using a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.g" text-decoration="underline">&lt;g&gt;</basic-link> element, whose <inline font-style="italic">ref</inline> attribute might have a value <inline>#air</inline> to link to the following simple definition for the symbol concerned : <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;char xml:id="air"&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;charName&gt;</inline>ALCHEMICAL SYMBOL FOR AIR<inline>&lt;/charName&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;mapping type="standard"&gt;</inline>🜁<inline>&lt;/mapping&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/char&gt;</inline>
            </block> Further details of these and related elements are provided in section <basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/WD.html#D25-20)">http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/WD.html#D25-20</basic-link> of the TEI Guidelines.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="profDesc"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="14pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="3pt"
                space-before.optimum="9pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.3. The Profile Description</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.profileDesc" text-decoration="underline">&lt;profileDesc&gt;</basic-link> element gathers together information about various descriptive aspects of a text. It has the following optional components: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.creation" text-decoration="underline">creation</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains information about the creation of a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.abstract" text-decoration="underline">abstract</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a summary or formal abstract prefixed to an existing source document by the encoder.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.particDesc" text-decoration="underline">particDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (participation description) describes the identifiable speakers, voices, or other participants in any kind of text or other persons named or otherwise referred to in a text, edition, or metadata.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.settingDesc" text-decoration="underline">settingDesc</basic-link>
                        </inline> (setting description) describes the setting or settings within which a language interaction takes place, or other places otherwise referred to in a text, edition, or metadata.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.langUsage" text-decoration="underline">langUsage</basic-link>
                        </inline> (language usage) describes the languages, sublanguages, registers, dialects, etc. represented within a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.textClass" text-decoration="underline">textClass</basic-link>
                        </inline> (text classification) groups information which describes the nature or topic of a text in terms of a standard classification scheme, thesaurus, etc.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.creation" text-decoration="underline">&lt;creation&gt;</basic-link> element documents where a work was created, even though it may not have been published or recorded there:</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;creation&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;date when="1992-08"&gt;</inline>August 1992<inline>&lt;/date&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;name type="place"&gt;</inline>Taos, New Mexico<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/creation&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.abstract" text-decoration="underline">&lt;abstract&gt;</basic-link> element may be used to provide a brief summary or abstract of the document concerned. It is most usually applied to texts born digital: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;profileDesc&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;abstract&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>This paper is a draft studying various aspects of using the TEI as a reference
     serialization framework for LMF. Comments are welcome to bring this to a useful
     document for the community.<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/abstract&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/profileDesc&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.particDesc" text-decoration="underline">&lt;particDesc&gt;</basic-link> element is used to list descriptive information about the real or fictional participants in a text, for example the characters in a novel or a play. It contains at least one <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listPerson" text-decoration="underline">&lt;listPerson&gt;</basic-link> element, which contains individual <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.person" text-decoration="underline">&lt;person&gt;</basic-link> elements.<list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listPerson" text-decoration="underline">listPerson</basic-link>
                        </inline> (list of persons) contains a list of descriptions, each of which provides information about an identifiable person or a group of people, for example the participants in a language interaction, or the people referred to in a historical source.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.person" text-decoration="underline">person</basic-link>
                        </inline> provides information about an identifiable individual, for example a participant in a language interaction, or a person referred to in a historical source.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block> For example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;profileDesc&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;particDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;listPerson&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;person xml:id="OPI"&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>
     <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>Dr Opimian<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>: named for the famous Roman fine wine.<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;/person&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;person xml:id="GRM"&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>
     <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>Mr Gryll<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>: named for the mythical Gryllus, one of Ulysses'
         sailors transformed by Circe into a pig, who argues that he was happier in
         that state than as a man.<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;/person&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/listPerson&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/particDesc&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/profileDesc&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">In the same way, the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.settingDesc" text-decoration="underline">&lt;settingDesc&gt;</basic-link> element can be used to list descriptive information about the real or fictional places mentioned in a text. It contains at least one <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listPlace" text-decoration="underline">&lt;listPlace&gt;</basic-link> element, which contains individual <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.place" text-decoration="underline">&lt;place&gt;</basic-link> elements. <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listPlace" text-decoration="underline">listPlace</basic-link>
                        </inline> (list of places) contains a list of places, optionally followed by a list of relationships (other than containment) defined amongst them.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.place" text-decoration="underline">place</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains data about a geographic location</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block> For example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;profileDesc&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;settingDesc&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;listPlace&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;head&gt;</inline>Houses mentioned in <inline>&lt;title&gt;</inline>Pride and Prejudice<inline>&lt;/title&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;/head&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;place xml:id="NETF1"&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>
     <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>Netherfield Park<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>: home of the Bingleys<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;/place&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;place xml:id="PEMB1"&gt;</inline>
    <inline>&lt;p&gt;</inline>
     <inline>&lt;name&gt;</inline>Pemberley<inline>&lt;/name&gt;</inline>: home of Mr Darcy<inline>&lt;/p&gt;</inline>
   <inline>&lt;/place&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;/listPlace&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/settingDesc&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/profileDesc&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The full TEI Guidelines provide a rich range of additional elements to define more structured information about persons and places; these are not however available in TEI Simple.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.langUsage" text-decoration="underline">&lt;langUsage&gt;</basic-link> element is useful where a text contains many different languages. It may contain <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.language" text-decoration="underline">&lt;language&gt;</basic-link> elements to document each particular language used: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.language" text-decoration="underline">language</basic-link>
                        </inline> characterizes a single language or sublanguage used within a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block> For example, a text containing predominantly text in French as spoken in Quebec, but also smaller amounts of British and Canadian English might be documented as follows: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;langUsage&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;language ident="fr-CA" usage="60"&gt;</inline>Québecois<inline>&lt;/language&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;language ident="en-CA" usage="20"&gt;</inline>Canadian Business English<inline>&lt;/language&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;language ident="en-GB" usage="20"&gt;</inline>British English<inline>&lt;/language&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/langUsage&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.textClass" text-decoration="underline">&lt;textClass&gt;</basic-link> element classifies a text. This may be done with reference to a classification system locally defined by means of the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.classDecl" text-decoration="underline">&lt;classDecl&gt;</basic-link> element, or by reference to some externally defined established scheme such as the Universal Decimal Classification. Texts may also be classified using lists of keywords, which may themselves be drawn from locally or externally defined control lists. The following elements are used to supply such classifications: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.classCode" text-decoration="underline">classCode</basic-link>
                        </inline> (classification code) contains the classification code used for this text in some standard classification system.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.catRef" text-decoration="underline">catRef</basic-link>
                        </inline> (category reference) specifies one or more defined categories within some taxonomy or text typology.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.keywords" text-decoration="underline">keywords</basic-link>
                        </inline> contains a list of keywords or phrases identifying the topic or nature of a text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The simplest way of classifying a text is by means of the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.classCode" text-decoration="underline">&lt;classCode&gt;</basic-link> element. For example, a text with classification 410 in the Universal Decimal Classification might be documented as follows: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;classCode scheme="http://www.udc.org"&gt;</inline>410<inline>&lt;/classCode&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">When a classification scheme has been locally defined using the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.taxonomy" text-decoration="underline">&lt;taxonomy&gt;</basic-link> element discussed in the preceding subsection, the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.catRef" text-decoration="underline">&lt;catRef&gt;</basic-link> element should be used to reference it. To continue the earlier example, a work classified in the Brown Corpus as <inline>Press reportage - Sunday</inline> and also as <inline>Religion</inline> might be documented as follows: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;catRef target="#B.A3 #B.D"/&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The element <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.keywords" text-decoration="underline">&lt;keywords&gt;</basic-link> contains one or more keywords or phrases identifying the topic or nature of a text, each tagged as a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.term" text-decoration="underline">&lt;term&gt;</basic-link>. As usual, the attribute <inline font-style="italic">scheme</inline> identifies the source from which these terms are taken. For example, if the LC Subject Headings are used, following declaration of that classification system in a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.taxonomy" text-decoration="underline">&lt;taxonomy&gt;</basic-link> element as above: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;textClass&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;keywords scheme="#LCSH"&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;term&gt;</inline>English literature<inline>&lt;/term&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;term&gt;</inline>History and criticism<inline>&lt;/term&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;term&gt;</inline>Data processing.<inline>&lt;/term&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/keywords&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/textClass&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Multiple classifications may be supplied using any of the mechanisms described in this section.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e5897"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="14pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="3pt"
                space-before.optimum="9pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.4. Other forms of metadata</block>
         <block line-height="1">The TEI header was one of the first attempts to provide a full range of metadata elements, but it is by no means the only standard now used for this purpose. To facilitate the management of large digital collections and to simplify interoperability of TEI and non-TEI resources, the following element may be found useful: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.xenoData" text-decoration="underline">xenoData</basic-link>
                        </inline> (non-TEI metadata) provides a container element into which metadata in non-TEI formats may be placed.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">A typical use for this element might be to store a set of descriptors conforming to the Dublin Core standard in the TEI header rather than to generate them automatically from the corresponding TEI elements. For examples and discussion, see the TEI Guidelines at <basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/HD.html#HD9)">http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/HD.html#HD9</basic-link>
         </block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="d27e5917"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="14pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="3pt"
                space-before.optimum="9pt"
                text-indent="0em">15.5. The Revision Description</block>
         <block line-height="1">The <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.revisionDesc" text-decoration="underline">&lt;revisionDesc&gt;</basic-link> element provides a change log in which each significant change made to a text may be recorded. It is always the last element in a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.teiHeader" text-decoration="underline">&lt;teiHeader&gt;</basic-link> and contains the following elements: <list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="18pt"
                        provisional-label-separation="6pt"
                        text-indent="0em"
                        margin-right="10pt"
                        space-before="6pt"
                        space-after="6pt">
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.change" text-decoration="underline">change</basic-link>
                        </inline> documents a change or set of changes made during the production of a source document, or during the revision of an electronic file.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
               <list-item space-before.optimum="4pt">
                  <list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <block text-align="end">•</block>
                  </list-item-label>
                  <list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <block font-weight="normal">
                        <inline font-weight="bold">
                           <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listChange" text-decoration="underline">listChange</basic-link>
                        </inline> groups a number of change descriptions associated with either the creation of a source text or the revision of an encoded text.</block>
                  </list-item-body>
               </list-item>
            </list-block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Each <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.change" text-decoration="underline">&lt;change&gt;</basic-link> element contains a brief description of a significant change. The attributes <inline font-style="italic">when</inline> and <inline font-style="italic">who</inline> may be used to identify when the change was carried out and the person responsible for it.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">It is good practice (but not required) to group changes together within a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.listChange" text-decoration="underline">&lt;listChange&gt;</basic-link> element.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Example: <block font-family="Courier"
                   background-color="lightgray"
                   color="black"
                   white-space-treatment="preserve"
                   linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                   white-space-collapse="false"
                   wrap-option="no-wrap"
                   text-indent="0em"
                   hyphenate="false"
                   start-indent="12pt"
                   text-align="start"
                   font-size="6pt"
                   space-before.optimum="4pt"
                   space-after.optimum="4pt">
               <inline>&lt;revisionDesc&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;listChange&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;change when="1991-11-11" who="#LB"&gt;</inline>deleted chapter 10<inline>&lt;/change&gt;</inline>
  <inline>&lt;change when="1991-11-02" who="#MSM"&gt;</inline>completed first draft<inline>&lt;/change&gt;</inline>
 <inline>&lt;/listChange&gt;</inline>
               <inline>&lt;/revisionDesc&gt;</inline>
            </block>
         </block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">In a production environment it will usually be found preferable to use some kind of automated system to track and record changes. Many such <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">version control systems</inline>, as they are known, can also be configured to update the TEI header of a file automatically.</block>
         <block keep-with-next.within-page="always"
                id="processingmodel"
                text-align="left"
                font-family="Times"
                font-size="18pt"
                font-weight="bold"
                space-after="6pt"
                space-before.optimum="12pt"
                text-indent="0em">16. The Simple Processing Model</block>
         <block line-height="1">Unlike most other TEI customizations, TEI simplePrint includes documentation of the intended processing associated with the majority of elements. As noted above, the TEI provides components such as the <inline font-style="italic">rendition</inline> attribute to indicate the appearance of particular parts of a document in the non-digital source from which it is derived. With TEI simplePrint, it is also possible to indicate how in general an element should be processed, in particular its intended appearance when processed for display on a screen or on paper. This ability derives from a number of capabilities recently added to the TEI architecture for the specification of processing, which were developed as part of the project that defined the TEI simplePrint schema.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">The key feature of this ‘Processing Model’ is a notation that allows the encoder to associate each element with one or more categories, which we call its <inline font-style="italic" font-weight="normal">behaviour</inline>s. In addition, the Processing Model indicates how the element should be rendered, possibly differently in differing circumstances, using the W3C Cascading Style Sheets (CSS) mentioned above. It is consequently much easier to develop processors for documents conforming to TEI simplePrint, since the complexity of the task is much reduced.</block>
         <block line-height="1"
                text-indent="1em"
                space-before.optimum="0pt"
                space-before.maximum="12pt">Twenty-five different behaviours are currently defined by the TEI Processing Model. Their names indicate informally the categorization concerned, and should be readily comprehensible for most programmers. The following table indicates the TEI simplePrint elements associated with each:</block>
         <table text-align="left"
                font-size="9pt"
                table-layout="fixed"
                width="100%"
                id="d27e5987">
            <table-body text-indent="0pt">
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell background-color="silver" padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block font-weight="bold">Behaviour</block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell background-color="silver" padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block font-weight="bold">Used by</block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell background-color="silver" padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block font-weight="bold">Effect</block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>alternate</block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>choice date</block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>support display of alternative visualizations, for example by displaying the preferred content, by displaying both in parallel, or by toggling between the two.</block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>anchor</block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>anchor </block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>create an identifiable anchor point in the output. </block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>block</block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>address addrLine argument back body byline closer dateline div docTitle epigraph figure floatingText formula front fw group head imprimatur l lg listBibl note opener postscript q quote role roleDesc salute signed sp speaker spGrp stage titlePage titlePart trailer </block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>create a block structure</block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>body</block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell padding="2pt" text-align="left">
                     <block>text </block>
                  </table-cell>
