                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-end-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <block line-height="1">The <inline font-style="italic">who</inline> attribute may be used to point to any other element, but will typically specify a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.respStmt" text-decoration="underline">&lt;respStmt&gt;</basic-link> or <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.person" text-decoration="underline">&lt;person&gt;</basic-link> element elsewhere in the header, identifying the person responsible for the change and their role in making it.</block>
                        <block line-height="1"
                               text-indent="1em"
                               space-before.optimum="0pt"
                               space-before.maximum="12pt">It is recommended that changes be recorded with the most recent first. The <inline font-style="italic">status</inline> attribute may be used to indicate the status of a document following the change documented.</block>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
