                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-end-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <block line-height="1">This element should be used for deletion of shorter sequences of text, typically single words or phrases. The <inline hyphenate="false" color="black" font-family="Courier">&lt;delSpan&gt;</inline> element should be used for longer sequences of text, for those containing structural subdivisions, and for those containing overlapping additions and deletions.</block>
                        <block line-height="1"
                               text-indent="1em"
                               space-before.optimum="0pt"
                               space-before.maximum="12pt">The text deleted must be at least partially legible in order for the encoder to be able to transcribe it (unless it is restored in a <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.supplied" text-decoration="underline">&lt;supplied&gt;</basic-link> tag). Illegible or lost text within a deletion may be marked using the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.gap" text-decoration="underline">&lt;gap&gt;</basic-link> tag to signal that text is present but has not been transcribed, or is no longer visible. Attributes on the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.gap" text-decoration="underline">&lt;gap&gt;</basic-link> element may be used to indicate how much text is omitted, the reason for omitting it, etc. If text is not fully legible, the <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.unclear" text-decoration="underline">&lt;unclear&gt;</basic-link> element (available when using the additional tagset for transcription of primary sources) should be used to signal the areas of text which cannot be read with confidence in a similar way.</block>
                        <block line-height="1"
                               text-indent="1em"
                               space-before.optimum="0pt"
                               space-before.maximum="12pt">Degrees of uncertainty over what can still be read, or whether a deletion was intended may be indicated by use of the <inline hyphenate="false" color="black" font-family="Courier">&lt;certainty&gt;</inline> element (see <basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/CE.html#CE)">21. Certainty, Precision, and Responsibility</basic-link>).</block>
                        <block line-height="1"
                               text-indent="1em"
                               space-before.optimum="0pt"
                               space-before.maximum="12pt">There is a clear distinction in the TEI between <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.del" text-decoration="underline">&lt;del&gt;</basic-link> and <inline hyphenate="false" color="black" font-family="Courier">&lt;surplus&gt;</inline> on the one hand and <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.gap" text-decoration="underline">&lt;gap&gt;</basic-link> or <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.unclear" text-decoration="underline">&lt;unclear&gt;</basic-link> on the other. <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.del" text-decoration="underline">&lt;del&gt;</basic-link> indicates a deletion present in the source being transcribed, which states the author's or a later scribe's intent to cancel or remove text. <inline hyphenate="false" color="black" font-family="Courier">&lt;surplus&gt;</inline> indicates material present in the source being transcribed which should have been so deleted, but which is not in fact. <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.gap" text-decoration="underline">&lt;gap&gt;</basic-link> or <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.unclear" text-decoration="underline">&lt;unclear&gt;</basic-link>, by contrast, signal an editor's or encoder's decision to omit something or their inability to read the source text. See sections <basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html#PHOM)">11.3.1.7. Text Omitted from or Supplied in the Transcription</basic-link> and <basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html#PHCOMB)">11.3.3.2. Use of the gap, del, damage, unclear, and supplied Elements in Combination</basic-link> for the relationship between these and other related elements used in detailed transcription.</block>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
