                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-end-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <block line-height="1">May be used to indicate that a passage is distinguished from the surrounding text for reasons concerning which no claim is made. When used in this manner, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.q" text-decoration="underline">&lt;q&gt;</basic-link> may be thought of as syntactic sugar for <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.hi" text-decoration="underline">&lt;hi&gt;</basic-link> with a value of <inline font-style="italic">rend</inline> that indicates the use of such mechanisms as quotation marks.</block>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
