                     <block>
                        <block font-family="Courier"
                               background-color="lightgray"
                               color="black"
                               white-space-treatment="preserve"
                               linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                               white-space-collapse="false"
                               wrap-option="no-wrap"
                               text-indent="0em"
                               hyphenate="false"
                               start-indent="12pt"
                               text-align="start"
                               font-size="6pt"
                               space-before.optimum="4pt"
                               space-after.optimum="4pt">Lexicography has shown little sign of being affected by the
 work of followers of J.R. Firth, probably best summarized in his
 slogan, <inline>&lt;quote&gt;</inline>You shall know a word by the company it
 keeps<inline>&lt;/quote&gt;</inline>
                           <inline>&lt;ref&gt;</inline>(Firth, 1957)<inline>&lt;/ref&gt;</inline>
                        </block>
                     </block>
