                     <block>
                        <block line-height="1">The <inline hyphenate="false" color="black" font-family="Courier">&lt;damage&gt;</inline>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.gap" text-decoration="underline">&lt;gap&gt;</basic-link>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.del" text-decoration="underline">&lt;del&gt;</basic-link>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.unclear" text-decoration="underline">&lt;unclear&gt;</basic-link> and <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.supplied" text-decoration="underline">&lt;supplied&gt;</basic-link> elements may be closely allied in use. See section <basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html#PHCOMB)">11.3.3.2. Use of the gap, del, damage, unclear, and supplied Elements in Combination</basic-link> for discussion of which element is appropriate for which circumstance.</block>
