               <table-row>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <inline font-weight="bold">Note</inline>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-end-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <block line-height="1">The same element is used for all cases of uncertainty in the transcription of element content, whether for written or spoken material. For other aspects of certainty, uncertainty, and reliability of tagging and transcription, see chapter <basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/CE.html#CE)">21. Certainty, Precision, and Responsibility</basic-link>.</block>
                        <block line-height="1"
                               text-indent="1em"
                               space-before.optimum="0pt"
                               space-before.maximum="12pt">The <inline hyphenate="false" color="black" font-family="Courier">&lt;damage&gt;</inline>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.gap" text-decoration="underline">&lt;gap&gt;</basic-link>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.del" text-decoration="underline">&lt;del&gt;</basic-link>, <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.unclear" text-decoration="underline">&lt;unclear&gt;</basic-link> and <basic-link internal-destination="TEI.supplied" text-decoration="underline">&lt;supplied&gt;</basic-link> elements may be closely allied in use. See section <basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html#PHCOMB)">11.3.3.2. Use of the gap, del, damage, unclear, and supplied Elements in Combination</basic-link> for discussion of which element is appropriate for which circumstance.</block>
                        <block line-height="1"
                               text-indent="1em"
                               space-before.optimum="0pt"
                               space-before.maximum="12pt">The <inline font-style="italic">hand</inline> attribute points to a definition of the hand concerned, as further discussed in section <basic-link external-destination="url(http://www.tei-c.org/release/doc/tei-p5-doc/en/html/PH.html#PHDH)">11.3.2.1. Document Hands</basic-link>.</block>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <inline font-weight="bold">Example</inline>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-end-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <block font-family="Courier"
                               background-color="lightgray"
                               color="black"
                               white-space-treatment="preserve"
                               linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                               white-space-collapse="false"
                               wrap-option="no-wrap"
                               text-indent="0em"
                               hyphenate="false"
                               start-indent="12pt"
                               text-align="start"
                               font-size="6pt"
                               space-before.optimum="4pt"
                               space-after.optimum="4pt">
                           <inline>&lt;u&gt;</inline> ...and then <inline>&lt;unclear reason="background-noise"&gt;</inline>Nathalie<inline>&lt;/unclear&gt;</inline> said ... <inline>&lt;/u&gt;</inline>
                        </block>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <inline font-weight="bold">Content model</inline>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-end-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <block font-family="Courier"
                               background-color="lightgray"
                               color="black"
                               white-space-treatment="preserve"
                               linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                               white-space-collapse="false"
                               wrap-option="no-wrap"
                               text-indent="0em"
                               hyphenate="false"
                               start-indent="12pt"
                               text-align="start"
                               font-size="6pt"
                               space-before.optimum="4pt"
                               space-after.optimum="4pt">
&lt;content&gt;
 &lt;macroRef key="macro.paraContent"/&gt;
&lt;/content&gt;
    </block>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
               </table-row>
               <table-row>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <inline font-weight="bold">Schema Declaration</inline>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
                  <table-cell border-after-style="solid"
                              border-end-style="solid"
                              border-start-style="solid"
                              padding="2pt"
                              text-align="left">
                     <block>
                        <block font-family="Courier"
                               background-color="lightgray"
                               color="black"
                               white-space-treatment="preserve"
                               linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                               white-space-collapse="false"
                               wrap-option="no-wrap"
                               text-indent="0em"
                               hyphenate="false"
                               start-indent="12pt"
                               text-align="start"
                               font-size="6pt"
                               space-before.optimum="4pt"
                               space-after.optimum="4pt">
element unclear
{
   att.global.attributes,
   att.editLike.attributes,
   attribute reason { list { + } }?,
   attribute agent { text }?,
   macro.paraContent
}</block>
                     </block>
                  </table-cell>
